{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports a [validation error](validators.md#habeas-req-requirements.sdk.graph.validators.ValidationError).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test sources only. I did not request any implementation source.\n\n**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.execute`**\n1. `Criterion::execute` takes `self` and a `&mut ValidationContext` for the criterion's source node. Reads and agent calls go through that context.\n2. It returns a `Send` future.\n3. `Ok` carries the completed answer, as defined by `criterion_trait.answer`. That answer includes a negative assessment, and its Serde form must round-trip.\n4. `Err` carries a `ValidationError<D::Error>`.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Ok answer, source-node context, dependencies.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` runs a deterministic criterion. It asserts the negative `result` and the rationale. It also asserts that the recorded dependency is `Node(1, fingerprint)`, which shows the context read the source node.\n  - `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` runs an SDK criterion that returns a negative answer (`determination: false`). It asserts `source_node_id`, then checks that the stored record equals the output. It also checks that a reloaded record has non-empty dependencies and gives back the same output, with only one agent request.\n- **Send.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` passes verification, storing and refreshing through a `send(...)` helper. That helper is a compile-time `Send` check, so a non-`Send` future would fail to compile. The same test asserts the answers (17, 23) and the execution counts.\n- **Negative answer is `Ok`, plus decode error.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` implements a custom `Criterion::execute` that reads the source node through `cx`.\n  - Invalid JSON gives `Err(ValidationError::Output)`, and nothing is stored.\n  - `false` gives `Ok(false)`, with dependency `Node(1, fp(\"false\"))`. Storing it records `json!(false)`, so the answer round-trips through Serde.\n- **Err variants.**\n  - `fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` covers `NoAgentConfigured` and then a successful run with an intermediate agent call.\n  - `fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` covers `Graph(\"missing\")` returned from execute and checks that no record is stored.\n  - `fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` covers `Agent(_)` returned from execute.\n  - `fn[agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload]` checks the error payload shape.\n\n**Gaps considered.** I found no obligation that lacks a test with an outcome assertion. Success and each error class are exercised and asserted. The negative-answer case is covered, and the `Send` bound is enforced at compile time. The source-node context is evidenced by the dependency assertions. I found no ambiguity in the text that leads to different conclusions. There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
  "references": "92f00a7a9b1677fe86e0dd6cd5850a82acfa0772e140f9a501f5db2552c605a9",
